<title>JAPAN: Japan Dec copper cable shipments up, orders down.</title>
<headline>Japan Dec copper cable shipments up, orders down.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese copper wire and cable shipments rose slightly in December from the same month last year, although orders edged downward, the Japanese Electric Wire and Cable Makers' Association said on Friday.</p>
<p>The preliminary December data and revised November data were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   Dec 96     yr/yr change	Nov 96 (revised)</p>
<p> Orders	  84,400	 -1.6 pct	  94,050  (+4.6 pct)</p>
<p>   Exports	3,700	 -0.2 pct	   4,509 (+13.0 pct)</p>
<p> Shipments     86,400	 +1.3 pct	  91,773  (+0.7 pct)</p>
<p>   Constr'n    34,000	 +5.8 pct	  34,670  (+5.3 pct)</p>
<p>   Electrical  22,900	 -0.6 pct	  23,840  (-4.2 pct)</p>
<p>   Elec Power   9,200	-10.9 pct	  10,887  (-8.2 pct)</p>
<p>   Automobile   6,300	+20.9 pct	   6,769 (+25.6 pct)</p>
<p>   Telecomms    3,200	+17.2 pct	   3,285  (+0.2 pct)</p>
<p>   Exports	3,900	-17.6 pct	   4,447  (-0.5 pct)</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
